<task id="to_add_the_excel_app_setup_button_in_salesforce_f2a6fd" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>To add the Excel App Setup button in Salesforce</title>
   <shortdesc>Designers must have the Excel App Setup button added to their layout on the Apps</shortdesc>
   <prolog>
      <author type="creator">Rakesh Singh</author>
       <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Salesforce</keyword>
        <keyword>Excel</keyword>
        <keyword>Setup</keyword>
        <keyword>button</keyword>
        <keyword>Apps</keyword>
        <keyword>List</keyword>
        <indexterm>Salesforce</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Excel</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Setup</indexterm>
      </keywords>
          <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <context>
         <p>Designers must have the Excel App Setup button added to their layout on the Apps List view to use the Launch from Salesforce feature.</p>
      </context>
      <steps>
         <step>
            <cmd>Log in to Salesforce and go to <b>Setup &gt; Create &gt; Objects</b> and click <b>App</b>.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>From the top of the page, click <b>Search Layouts.</b>
            </cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668051</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667667/98668051.png" width="869" height="206" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Edit</b> next to Apps List View and move Excel App Setup to Selected Buttons.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668050</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667667/98668050.png" width="345" height="267" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Save</b>.</cmd>
         </step>
      </steps>
      <result>
         <ul>
            <li>For step-by-step instructions on launching an app from Salesforce, refer to <xref href="../launching_an_x_author_for_exce_98667728/launching_an_xauthor_for_excel_app_from_salesforce.dita">Launching an X-Author for Excel App from Salesforce</xref>.</li>
            <li>For step-by-step instructions on activating and assigning apps, refer to <xref href="/pages/createpage.action?spaceKey=XAEWIN18&amp;title=Activating+and+Assigning+Apps+in+Salesforce&amp;linkCreation=true&amp;fromPageId=98667667">Activating and Assigning Apps in Salesforce</xref>.</li>
         </ul>
      </result>
   </taskbody>
</task>